## Test Command Inference

- **Node.js**: If `pnpm-lock.yaml` exists → `pnpm test`; if `yarn.lock` exists → `yarn test`; else `npm test`. Prefer coverage when configured (e.g., `-- --coverage`).
- **Python**: If `pyproject.toml` exists → prefer `pytest`; if `tox.ini` exists → run `tox`; otherwise `pytest`.
- **Go**: `go test ./... -race -cover`
- **Rust**: `cargo test --all --all-features` when applicable
- **Java**: If `mvnw` or `pom.xml` exists → `./mvnw -q test` or `mvn -q test`; if `gradlew` or `build.gradle*` exists → `./gradlew test`
- **.NET**: `dotnet test` (solution or project root)
- **Ruby**: If `Gemfile` exists and `spec/` directory → `bundle exec rspec`; else `rake test`
- **PHP**: If `vendor/bin/phpunit` exists → `vendor/bin/phpunit`
- **Elixir**: `mix test`
- **Fallback**: Run repository's documented test command from README or CI config (e.g., `.github/workflows/*.yml`)

Always run tests before committing. If tests fail, do not commit until fixed.
